Today is Friday evening, and I am at home.
Someone knocks on my door.
I open the door.
Outside stands my neighbour, Asha.
With her is her dog, Moti.
In Asha's hand is a heavy bag.
In that bag is the dog's food.
In her other hand is the dog's leash.
Asha smiles and says to me.
"Maya, thank you very much."
"I am going out of town this weekend."
"You are helping me, so I am happy."
I smile and look at him.
He wags his tail with excitement.
I say, "No problem, Asha."
"Please bring him inside."
Asha brings that heavy bag inside the house.
She places the bag on the floor.
She says, "His food is in this bag."
"You must look after him well over the weekend."
